WEBVTT

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:16.340
Join our forces with ISDA's military division?

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.120
Yes, I believe it will be a good
chance to show to the world

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.350
the power of the Girouard.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.620
All right. I believe I will take you up on that.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.600
In that event, we will need
someone to head it up.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.870
I think Prince Rasina would be well-suited.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.860
Hmm, I believe you're right.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.320
Something terrible has happened!

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.310
It's Rasina-sama... Prince Rasina has been!

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.910
In my younger days, I lost

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:24.810
even the reason for this pain

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.520
Crouching over, making excuses

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.720
I must have...

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:41.430
Taking hold of the premonition
I saw at the end of the blue,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:49.000
riding the wind, I'm off
to where the light shines

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.870
I'll always be with you

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.380
see the sky in front of you

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.750
fly high in a light from the deepest blue

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:06.090
Riding the echo of swirling stars,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.760
I sing out

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:17.430
May my voice reach you

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.890
Gio!

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.680
You owe me one for that.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.250
I'll pay you back right away.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.580
They just keep coming!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.850
No matter what might stand
in my way, I will reach Toa!

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.770
The second wave has been wiped out.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.800
Third wave is approaching the
Dragons and entering battle.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.270
Dispatch the Agathion squad!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.640
There's no need for that.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.310
But Your Highness, they are
surely coming this way

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.980
to take back the Album.
Before they can do that...

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.890
Why don't we invite them in?
That sounds more entertaining.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.820
But, Your Highness!

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.290
Garnet!

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.190
As you wish.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.990
Hey, now,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.920
here I thought we were finally
making a charge at Thanatos,

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.330
and we're taking a break
already? That's not right!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.260
Don't be in such a rush, Howling Star.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:32.500
Let's get going!
I'm itching all over for a fight!

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.100
I'm counting on that.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.370
Say...

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.610
...how long are we going to be on the Moon?

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.240
As long as it takes for the
Avenir's final inspection,

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.710
and to load the Type-X.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.780
Oh...

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.030
As a result of the Ostrum's
attack the other day,

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:07.240
the threat posed by Thanatos has
suddenly become a lot more real.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.070
People are pushing and shoving
their way to get to the spaceport,

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.410
because they want to get away from Earth.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.140
Violence is breaking out all over.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.310
There was nothing we could do
to prevent Shin-Ogasawara City

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:23.250
from being destroyed
because of the Original Dragons.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:27.090
Some are saying that ISDA is responsible.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.890
Mister Cyril, how do you plan
to explain this screw-up?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.930
Just a moment, please! If the Girouard Force

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.670
hadn't ignored our request for
assistance in the first place...

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:41.940
Are you saying that we are
responsible for the city's destruction?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.610
Are you saying you aren't?

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.140
Isn't it terribly dishonorable
to place the blame

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.980
for your own faults onto someone else?

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:55.350
How can you dare say that?!
Do you know how much trouble

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:59.120
we've had to put up with lately
because of the Girouard Force?!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.020
Calm down, Mister Cyril!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.130
Remember, you are speaking
to the king of a nation!

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.100
The infighting within D Project also
led to the failure of the operation.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.940
It is important that we all
remain unified, first and foremost.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.970
The conflict with ISDA was a result

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.980
of Asim and some of his
officers acting on their own.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.610
We are having trouble controlling him.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:29.180
It is Prince Asim that has
control of your military, isn't it?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:34.790
That is not true. The final
authority ultimately rests with me.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.390
I promise you, from now on,

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:40.950
the Girouard Force will
support ISDA in all aspects.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.000
So you're not the only
ones who aren't unified...

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.670
How are you feeling?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:30.910
That look in your eyes is as nice
as ever. So filled with sorrow.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:37.120
It appears that ISDA is about
to launch an attack on your kind.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.050
Attack?

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.290
You can't let them go! If they do that,
there will be no going back!

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.300
Please! Let me out of here!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.430
No. You belong to me.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.700
If I don't do something,
Earth is going to be wiped out!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.610
That would be entertaining.
It's not often you get to watch

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:02.410
the moment when a planet is extinguished.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:06.650
Entertaining? Earth is
your home world, isn't it?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.450
How can you look so calm about this?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.920
What about you? Why are
you so worried about Earth?

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.790
You're a Dragon.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.950
W-Well...

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:22.160
Whether or not Earth is
destroyed, or however many

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.570
billions of people die, it doesn't
make any difference to me.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.500
What?!

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:31.140
People only think about themselves anyway.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.640
They're nothing but foolish creatures.

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:37.250
Foolish? You're a human, aren't you?!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.950
Yes. But I am a chosen human.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:45.790
A being that stands at the peak of all humanity.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.590
All life is equal, wherever it is.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.360
There are none greater or lesser than others.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.360
Moreover, I don't think that humans are foolish,

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.630
or think only of themselves.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:03.000
Ooh, a Dragon, speaking up for humans, huh?

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:08.480
Sometimes, people will let
their appetites run out of control.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:14.050
But people have...
people have love in their hearts!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.450
Love?

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.190
When they want to protect someone,

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.460
they are able to sacrifice themselves to do it.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.830
That's the love to care for
those who are dear to them.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.960
Sometimes, that gives rise
to unimaginably great power.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:32.200
Love... But that, too,
is one of man's appetites.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:35.340
One of man's ugly natures, isn't it?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:41.010
I believe in both that ugliness,
and the beauty of love.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:45.250
It's all a part of what being human is.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.920
The power that love gives rise to, eh?

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:51.850
Would that be Kamishina Jin you're referring to?

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:54.520
How do you know about Jin?

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:59.760
Allow me to let you in on something.
He will be here, very soon.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:04.420
No... Jin couldn't know that I'm here.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:09.670
Your Highness, he has appeared.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.210
Are you ready?

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.110
Everything is in place.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.240
He will be landing shortly.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.950
Is Jin really here?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.950
You said that love gives
rise to great power, right?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:26.720
Why don't you prove whether or not
that's true to your prince now?

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.370
There's a guidance signal coming from Mars.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.280
Is this a Girouard trap?

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.240
You'd be right to think so, huh?

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.080
Well, should we turn back?

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.150
Of course not! We have to go in!

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.140
That's more like it.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.010
I'm so bored! When are we going to attack?!

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.940
Not yet, Howling Star.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:25.140
Ahh, I'm starting to go soft!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.120
I wonder if they've safely gotten together yet.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:50.340
Targets will be entering
firing range momentarily.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.540
I'll turn them to space dust this time for sure!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.340
They are within firing range.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.710
Fire!!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.620
They're greeting us with some lavish fireworks!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.890
Let's go, Gio!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.690
3rd and 4th Blocks disabled.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:49.320
7th and 8th Blocks also disabled.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.560
Send in the Agathions!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.930
Jin, incoming!

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:14.450
We're going through them, Gio!

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.480
Akira, we're going straight on in!

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.150
Yeah!

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.210
Don't let them near the dome!

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.720
Akira!

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:57.800
Leave this to us!

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:03.930
Akira...

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.110
That's right. Just keep on going,

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.670
Jin!

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.450
It's now or never!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.190
Wow, not bad.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.970
Gio...

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:52.720
Activating emergency bulwarks!

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:56.120
Main lobby damaged! Reading two intruders!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.520
Toa! Where are you?!

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.370
Jin!

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:09.840
Ooh, first time I've seen that expression.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:17.840
Fascinating. I can't wait to see
what expression you show me next.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.720
- CSS!
- Gio!

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:38.770
Welcome to my castle.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:41.740
I am Asim, the one in charge here.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:43.600
Where is Toa?!

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:47.170
The captive princess is at the top of the tower.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:50.710
If you want to see her,
you'll have to come up here.

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:54.110
We'll see if you can make it here in one piece.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.040
Gio, are you okay?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.740
Yeah, more or less.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:48.070
- Jin!
- Aw, how ungraceful.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:51.270
See how foolish he looks?

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:54.260
You're the one who's foolish.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:17:00.310
How can you take pleasure
in watching people get hurt?

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:05.490
You are the most foolish creature of them all.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:10.420
So you can make that
angry face, too. How pretty.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.430
Jin, go on!

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.330
Toa...

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.310
Jin!

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.050
Move it!!

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.300
Gio!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.480
Jin!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:16.690
Please! Make it stop!

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:19.090
When it comes to Kamishina Jin,

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:22.700
you really do show a wide
variety of expressions, huh?

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.560
Almost as though you were human.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.230
Toa!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.110
Toa!

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.710
Jin!

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:50.590
I'm impressed you made it this far.

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:55.600
The power of love...
Apparently, it's not completely untrue.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.530
You let Toa out of there!

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.930
Let her out yourself.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.710
- Jin!
- Why, you!

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.750
Stay away from His Highness!

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:22.480
Move!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:30.260
Toa...

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:33.900
Is that all for the power of love?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.640
Stop! Asim!

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:39.270
That's more like it.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:42.270
Jin!

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:53.840
Magnificent! To think that your
love would amuse me this much!

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:05.800
My, my, it looks like you've lost consciousness.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.170
Give Toa... give Toa back!

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.040
Filthy creature!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.810
Stop!

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:25.510
Impossible... breaking that
special glass, in a CSS-field space?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.030
Highness!

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.670
- Toa...
- Jin...

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:07.990
Jin!

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.430
I came to get you.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.830
Thanks.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:26.270
You did it.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:35.690
The power of love, huh?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:39.750
Fascinating. Truly fascinating.

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:21.740
You don't even think hard about the meaning

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:24.000
of the words you spit out

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:28.340
you just run away from the present

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:30.610
Still doing the same things over and over,

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:32.750
like nothing has happened

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:36.420
It makes no sense to run away again

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:45.290
In the end, you're immature,
still a child, complacent

00:22:45.290 --> 00:22:54.700
Leave behind your old self already

00:22:54.700 --> 00:22:59.210
The righteous fight starts within you

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:03.640
What would you do?
You're out of time, aren't you?

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:08.720
Try to remember how you're supposed to be

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:15.820
before it all falls apart

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:21.950
Fight or flight

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:29.400
Fight or flight

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:46.490
Ryoko here. Have any of you
ever found a stray kitten?

00:23:46.490 --> 00:23:48.420
I just found one myself.

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:51.060
Saki here. I just found a stray puppy.

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:54.390
You two are such pushovers. I found this guy.

00:23:54.390 --> 00:23:57.160
- A-A giant crocodile?!
- Megumi, where did you find him?!

00:23:57.160 --> 00:23:59.270
He followed me here! Help!

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:00.900
Gah! Don't come this way!

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:03.100
Wait! Do the preview before you run away!

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:05.510
Huh? Next time, who'd have
thought that such a thing

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.010
would be in such a place?

00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:09.200
Run!!
